<% layout("/layouts/boilerplate") %>

<section class="disease-details-section">
    <div class="container">

        <div class="disease-breadcrumb">
            <a href="/">Home</a>
            <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-right"></i>
            <a href="/diseases">Disease & Pest</a>
            <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-right"></i>
            <span>Wheat Rust</span>
        </div>

        <div class="disease-details-header">

            <div class="disease-details-icon">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-virus"></i>
            </div>

            <div>
                <span class="disease-type">Disease</span>
                <h1>Wheat Rust</h1>
                <p>
                    A fungal disease that can affect wheat crops
                    and reduce crop growth and productivity.
                </p>
            </div>

        </div>

        <div class="disease-info-section">
            <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-seedling"></i>Affected Crop</h2>
            <div class="affected-crop-box">
                <strong>Wheat</strong>
                <span>Rabi Crop</span>
            </div>

        </div>

        <div class="disease-info-section">

            <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info"></i>Overview</h2>
            <p>
                Wheat rust refers to fungal diseases that can affect
                wheat plants. Different rust diseases may affect
                different parts of the plant and can influence
                crop development when conditions are favorable.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="disease-info-section">

            <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-eye"></i>Symptoms</h2>

            <ul class="disease-points">
                <li>
                    Rust-colored or orange-brown pustules may appear
                    on affected plant parts.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Symptoms can vary depending on the type of rust
                    and stage of crop development.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Severe infection may affect plant growth and
                    grain development.
                </li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="disease-info-section">

            <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-cloud-sun"></i>Favorable Conditions</h2>

            <p>
                Disease development can be influenced by factors such
                as temperature, humidity, rainfall and crop conditions.
                The exact conditions vary with the type of rust.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="disease-info-section">

            <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-magnifying-glass"></i>Identification</h2>
            <p>
                Identification should consider visible symptoms,
                crop stage and field conditions. For uncertain cases,
                farmers should seek confirmation from a qualified
                agricultural expert or local agricultural service.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="disease-info-section">

            <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-shield-halved"></i>General Management</h2>
            <ul class="disease-points">
                <li>
                    Use recommended agricultural practices suitable
                    for the crop and local conditions.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Monitor the crop regularly for early symptoms.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Follow locally recommended disease-management
                    practices when treatment is required.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Consult an agriculture expert when disease
                    identification or treatment is uncertain.
                </li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="disease-info-section">

            <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-check-circle"></i>Prevention</h2>

            <ul class="disease-points">
                <li>
                    Use healthy and recommended planting material.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Maintain proper crop management practices.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Regularly monitor the field for early symptoms.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Follow recommendations appropriate to the
                    local growing conditions.
                </li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="disease-advisor-cta">
            <div>
                <h2>Need help identifying a crop problem?</h2>
                <p>
                    Connect with an agriculture advisor for
                    personalized guidance.
                </p>
            </div>
            <a href="/advisors" class="btn btn-success">Find an Advisor<i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-right"></i></a>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>